    <summary>See HEIC, RAW, PDF and CAD thumbnails in File Explorer, plus a right-click menu to convert, resize and OCR images. Free, offline.</summary>
    <description><![CDATA[Your HEIC, camera RAW, PDF and CAD files finally show a picture in Windows File Explorer, and a right-click menu lets you convert, resize and copy text out of images without opening another program. Thumbwright is free, open source and never connects to the internet.

HEIC and HEIF photos are decoded by Thumbwright itself and need no Microsoft Store codec. AVIF and AVCI thumbnails need Microsoft's free AV1 and HEIF extensions from the Microsoft Store; Thumbwright draws the picture, Windows supplies the codec.

## Features

- **Thumbnails for 315 formats**: camera RAW (CR3, CR2, CRW, NEF, ARW, ORF, RW2, RAF, X3F, DNG and more), JPEG XL, JPEG 2000, HEIC/AVIF, Blender, Aseprite, GIMP XCF, PSD, Krita, SVG, DWG/DXF, FreeCAD, 3MF, G-code, PDF, EPUB, legacy Office, DjVu, ZIP/7z/RAR and CBZ/CBR comics, video frames, album art, Android APK icons and a long tail of scientific and legacy bitmaps.
- **Right-click tools**: convert, resize, lossless JPEG rotation, shrink for email, make a file smaller than a given size, copy text from an image (OCR), combine into PDF or comic book, rename by date or camera, sort into folders, wallpaper, lock screen and folder icon.
- **Thumbwright Workbench**: a Start menu shortcut opens the settings, where you choose file types and menu items.
- **Safe by design**: complex decoders run in a separate, locked-down process, so a malformed file cannot crash Explorer. Thumbwright never changes another program's file associations, and uninstall removes exactly what it added.
- Command-line tool `twctl` for every menu verb plus batch conversion and diagnostics (`twctl doctor`).

## Package parameters

Silent installs show no window. Two optional parameters preset the first run for users who have not saved settings yet (they are stored machine-wide and can be changed later in Thumbwright Workbench):

- `/Menu:0` starts with the right-click menu off (`/Menu:1`, the default, leaves it on).
- `/Kit:<name>` preselects a starter kit: `photos`, `paperwork`, `design`, `cad`, `thumbnails` or `everything`.

Example: `choco install thumbwright --params "'/Menu:0 /Kit:photos'"`. Pass the parameters again on `choco upgrade`; an upgrade without them clears the presets.

## Notes

- Installs per-machine to `Program Files\Thumbwright` (requires administrator).
- On Windows 11, right-click > App extensions > Thumbwright, or Shift + right-click for the full menu. You can pin Thumbwright to the top level from Customize menu. The Windows 11 entry appears after your next sign-in.
- Windows and other programs keep file types they already handle, so a few types (for example HEIC while another app owns it) can show that program's thumbnail instead. `twctl doctor` lists them.
]]></description>
